        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): handle main() rejections and non-EPIPE stream errors",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe CLI entrypoint floated `void main(process.argv)`, so unexpected\nrejections became unhandled promise rejections. Non-EPIPE stdout/stderr\nerrors threw from event listeners (uncaughtException). Diagnostics written\nwith `process.stderr.write` immediately before `process.exit` can also be\ntruncated on async pipes.\n\n## Evidence\n\nSpawned-process regression suite on the patched handlers:\n\n```console\n$ tsx --test test/cli-entrypoint.test.ts\n✔ handleMainRejection sets process.exitCode to 1\n✔ spawned handleMainRejection writes [acpx] diagnostic and exits 1\n✔ spawned handleStreamError EPIPE exits 0 without diagnostic\n✔ spawned handleStreamError non-EPIPE writes diagnostic and exits 1\n✔ writeFatalLine is usable when stderr is a pipe\nℹ tests 6\nℹ pass 6\nℹ fail 0\n\n$ node -e 'writeSync(2, \"[acpx] stream error: EIO on stdout\\n\"); process.exit(1)'\nexit_code=1\nstderr=\"[acpx] stream error: EIO on stdout\\n\"\n```\n\n## Summary\n\n- Catch top-level `main()` rejections; set `process.exitCode = 1`\n- Non-EPIPE stream errors: sync diagnostic via `writeSync(2, ...)` then `exit(1)`\n- EPIPE still exits 0\n- Export handlers + focused spawn tests\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** unhandled top-level main rejections and non-EPIPE stream throws; async write+exit truncation\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS, Node 22+, branch fix/cli-void-main-rejection, tsx test runner\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:** `tsx --test test/cli-entrypoint.test.ts`\n- **Evidence after fix:** terminal output above (diagnostics present, exit codes 0/1 as designed)\n- **Observed result after fix:** rejected main and non-EPIPE stream paths emit `[acpx]` lines and nonzero status; EPIPE stays 0\n- **What was not tested:** production agent sessions that hit rare stream errors mid-turn\n\n## Related\n\n- ClawSweeper P2: flush fatal diagnostics before exit\n- ClawSweeper P1: spawned-process regression coverage\n",
